@@ -155,6 +155,30 @@ The advisor runs on Coding Harness's `advisor` model role; point that role at
 another vendor to combine this with cross-vendor review. `task.agentAdvisor`
 turns it off or picks a model per agent.
 
+### Stream-time rules
+
+The adapter registers `.harness-aidlc/host/rules/` with Coding Harness's rule
+engine, which matches a tool call while the model is still streaming it. A rule
+with `interruptMode: tool-only` stops the call before it runs; `always` also
+stops prose; `never` lets the call through and injects the reminder afterwards.
+
+| Rule | Guards | When it fires | Mode |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `aidlc-no-stubs` | the definition of done | a code write throws `not implemented`, or contains `TODO: implement`, `raise NotImplementedError`, `unimplemented!()` or `todo!()` | `tool-only` |
+| `aidlc-state-files` | state discipline | any write or edit to `aidlc-state.md`, the intent registry, the active-intent pointer or an audit shard | `always` |
+| `aidlc-reviewer-readonly` | reviewer independence | a reviewer, product lead or compliance agent writes a code file | `always` |
+| `aidlc-evidence` | evidence before claims | the main agent or developer says work is done without citing a command it ran (judged by a small model) | `prose-only` |
+
+The adapter also derives a rule from the project's method. When a memory file
+the space includes has a line that rules out mocks (for example `Do not mock the
+database`), it writes `aidlc/.aidlc-sessions/harness/rules/aidlc-no-mocks.md`,
+which quotes that line whenever a test file calls `jest.mock`, `vi.mock`,
+`mock.module`, `mock.patch` or `MagicMock`. The rule only reminds
+(`interruptMode: never`) because a practice may allow some mocks. Remove the
+line from the method and the rule goes with it at the next session start.
+
+Try a rule offline with `harness ttsr test --rule <file> --source tool --tool write --path <path> -- '<snippet>'`.
+
 ## Alongside Claude Code
 
 One project can carry both distributions: run `aidlc config --harness claude`
