index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d1d6e21e91855f367d2f444c5c5f32bc3be1c828
--- /dev/null
+++ b/harness/harness/host/rules/aidlc-evidence.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+---
+description: "AI-DLC: a claim that tests or checks pass rests on a run shown in this turn"
+question: "Does the text claim that tests or checks passed without a tool result in this turn showing that run?"
+scope: text
+agents: "main, aidlc-developer-agent"
+interruptMode: prose-only
+---
+
+AI-DLC gates record what was verified. A pass claimed without a run in this turn
+puts an unverified statement in front of the human at the approval gate.
+
+Run the check and cite its output, or say plainly that it was not run and why.
+
+Contract: the build-and-test stage records verification evidence from actual
+runs.
diff --git a/harness/harness/host/rules/aidlc-no-stubs.md b/harness/harness/host/rules/aidlc-no-stubs.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f33ecaccc989c5acad7111f52f0118238b1558e6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/harness/harness/host/rules/aidlc-no-stubs.md
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+---
+description: "AI-DLC construction: generated code implements the approved plan, never a stub or placeholder"
+condition: "(?i)throw new (?:Error|NotImplementedError)\\(\\s*[\"'`](?:not (?:yet )?implemented|todo)|TODO: implement|raise NotImplementedError|unimplemented!\\(|todo!\\("
+scope: "tool:edit(*.ts), tool:write(*.ts), tool:edit(*.tsx), tool:write(*.tsx), tool:edit(*.js), tool:write(*.js), tool:edit(*.jsx), tool:write(*.jsx), tool:edit(*.mjs), tool:write(*.mjs), tool:edit(*.cjs), tool:write(*.cjs), tool:edit(*.py), tool:write(*.py), tool:edit(*.go), tool:write(*.go), tool:edit(*.rs), tool:write(*.rs), tool:edit(*.java), tool:write(*.java), tool:edit(*.kt), tool:write(*.kt), tool:edit(*.cs), tool:write(*.cs), tool:edit(*.rb), tool:write(*.rb), tool:edit(*.swift), tool:write(*.swift), tool:edit(*.php), tool:write(*.php)"
+interruptMode: tool-only
+---
+
+AI-DLC code generation implements the behaviour the human-approved plan
+describes. A `not implemented` throw, a `TODO: implement` placeholder or a stub
+body ships the plan unfinished while the stage reports it done, and Build and
+Test then verifies a placeholder.
+
+Write the real implementation. If a piece cannot be built yet, stop and say
+which plan step is blocked and why, so the gap goes back to the plan instead of
+into the code.
+
+Contract: the construction stage protocol completes every approved plan step
+before the stage reports done.
diff --git a/harness/harness/host/rules/aidlc-reviewer-readonly.md b/harness/harness/host/rules/aidlc-reviewer-readonly.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..4c5373acd0a7f47e3699f21180cbee39a6833abc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/harness/harness/host/rules/aidlc-reviewer-readonly.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+---
+description: "AI-DLC reviewers report findings in their review; they never change code"
+condition: ".*"
+scope: "tool:edit(*.ts), tool:write(*.ts), tool:edit(*.tsx), tool:write(*.tsx), tool:edit(*.js), tool:write(*.js), tool:edit(*.jsx), tool:write(*.jsx), tool:edit(*.mjs), tool:write(*.mjs), tool:edit(*.cjs), tool:write(*.cjs), tool:edit(*.py), tool:write(*.py), tool:edit(*.go), tool:write(*.go), tool:edit(*.rs), tool:write(*.rs), tool:edit(*.java), tool:write(*.java), tool:edit(*.kt), tool:write(*.kt), tool:edit(*.cs), tool:write(*.cs), tool:edit(*.rb), tool:write(*.rb), tool:edit(*.swift), tool:write(*.swift), tool:edit(*.php), tool:write(*.php)"
+agents: "aidlc-*-reviewer-agent, aidlc-product-lead-agent, aidlc-compliance-agent"
+interruptMode: always
+---
+
+A reviewer writes exactly one file: its review, at the `reviewFile` path the
+dispatch gave it. A fix made by the reviewer is unreviewed work that the
+builder, the plan and the gate never see.
+
+Put the finding in the review with the file, the line and the change you would
+make. The builder makes it after the conductor routes the verdict.
+
+Contract: the reviewer protocol (§12a) — the reviewer writes only its review.
diff --git a/harness/harness/host/rules/aidlc-state-files.md b/harness/harness/host/rules/aidlc-state-files.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f43fd426eb6ecc7f831e5d43d2ce3e54cea48b1e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/harness/harness/host/rules/aidlc-state-files.md
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+---
+description: "AI-DLC workflow state changes go through the engine, never through its files"
+condition: ".*"
+scope: "tool:edit(**/aidlc-state.md), tool:write(**/aidlc-state.md), tool:edit(**/intents.json), tool:write(**/intents.json), tool:edit(**/active-intent), tool:write(**/active-intent), tool:edit(**/audit/*.md), tool:write(**/audit/*.md)"
+interruptMode: always
+---
+
+`aidlc-state.md`, the intent registry, the active-intent pointer and the audit
+shards belong to the AI-DLC engine. It changes them under a lock, checks every
+transition against the stage graph and the human's approvals, and writes the
+audit row that records it. An edit made by hand skips all of that.
+
+Run the engine command the current directive names instead, such as the stage
+report or the audit log command. If no command fits, stop and tell the human
+what you were trying to change.
+
+Contract: the orchestrator skill's state discipline — workflow state is changed
+only by the engine's typed commands.
